.Rproj.user
.Rhistory
.RData
.RDataTmp*
.Ruserdata
# Litter from a headless `Rscript main.R`/`Rscript run_tests.R` run: dev.new() falls back to a
# default pdf() device when no display is available, auto-numbering Rplots1.pdf, Rplots2.pdf, ...
# on repeated calls (see Diagnostics.R's and run_tests.R's own comments on this). Not a real
# output -- has leaked into the working tree and gotten accidentally committed twice already.
Rplots*.pdf
*.csv
!tests/testthat/fixtures/**/*.csv
!israeli_cbs_wfh_2digit.csv

# Checkpoint 9: persisted output layer. Tracked in git (not blanket-ignored) -- these are derived
# from real CBS microdata and several breakdowns produce small cells by construction (e.g. the
# Arab-women-only stratified regression). The `*.csv` rule above would otherwise still catch every
# CSV in here, hence the negation. This removes the structural gitignore block, NOT the review
# requirement: per CLAUDE.md, nothing under outputs/ gets `git add`ed/committed without a human
# first explicitly reviewing it for disclosure risk. See docs/ROADMAP.md Checkpoint 9.
!outputs/**
